This repository is a packaging-focused source tree rather than an unpacked
upstream project checkout.

The Debian build flow in `debian/rules` does the following:

  * unpack `ubutils.tar.gz` into `debian/build-tree/ubutils`
  * apply the root-level openEuler patch files
  * configure and build the extracted source with CMake
  * stage `lsub`, `setub`, `ub.ids`, and generated man pages into the package

To build a binary package on a Debian 12 arm64 host:

  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

The standard Debian artifact name remains available for tooling, and the build
also emits a copy named like:

  ubutils_1.0.2_velinux_arm64.deb
